//- 4:00 HEEL MODE: the no path, out by 5:00. It sits after the yes path's end slide and is reached by the vote slide's No link or the X key. The ugly American and his food crimes, one line a slide, never Trump: docs/TALK.md, The heel, has the character and the guardrail.

//- The turn is a smash cut, so it lands while the room is still booing the vote. The Mexico mix-up runs through the tortilla and pays off at Taco Bell.
section#heel.over-media.is-shout(data-background-image="img/carihuela.jpg" data-transition="none" data-timing="8")
  h2 Hola, Mexico!
  cite.credit Photo: Jl FilpoC
  aside.notes
    ul
      li The turn. Don't explain it. Become the loudest American you've ever sat next to on a plane.
      li Pure heat from here. No recanting, no color.
      li La Carihuela, right here in Torremolinos.

section.over-media(data-background-image="img/paella-chorizo.jpg" data-timing="8")
  h2 I fixed your paella.
  cite.credit Photo: Ypsilon from Finland
  aside.notes
    ul
      li Chorizo. Jamie Oliver tried it on 4 October 2016 and Spain still hasn't forgiven him.
      li Also the bottom was burnt, so I sent it back. (The socarrat, the best part.)

section.over-media(data-background-image="img/tortilla.jpg" data-timing="8")
  h2 This tortilla is broken.
  cite.credit Photo: Tamorlan
  aside.notes
    ul
      li It's full of potatoes. Where do the beans go?
      li Onion or no onion? Neither. Ketchup. Both halves of the room boo at once.

section.over-media(data-background-image="img/espetos.jpg" data-timing="8")
  h2 You're doing fish sticks wrong.
  cite.credit Photo: Diego Delso
  aside.notes
    ul
      li Espetos, on the beach at La Malagueta. The most Málaga food there is.
      li In America the fish goes inside the stick. Breaded. Rectangular. Frozen. The way God intended.

//- Café Central's tile chart, shown whole like the Ishihara plate, with the caption on one line under it so it doesn't cover a cup.
section.over-media.portrait.is-figure.one-line(data-timing="8")
  img(src="img/cafe-central.jpg" alt="Café Central's tile chart of the ways to order a coffee in Málaga, from solo to nube")
  h2 Which one's a regular coffee?
  cite.credit Photo: Daniel Capilla
  aside.notes
    ul
      li Café Central's chart, from 1954. Nine ways to order a coffee in Málaga, and a tenth, "no me lo ponga", that means don't bother.
      li None of them is regular. I want twenty ounces, in paper, with a lid.

//- The clock is the room's real time (js/heel-clock.js), so the line works whenever the talk lands. The 20:14 is only there until the script runs.
section.statement.is-shout(data-timing="8")
  h2
    time.now 20:14
  p I ate at five.
  aside.notes
    ul
      li The clock is live. Read it out in the room's own 24-hour time and be appalled by it.
      li That's not a time. And nobody here has even had dinner yet. What is wrong with you people?

section.over-media(data-background-image="img/taco-bell.jpg" data-timing="7")
  h2 I'm going to get some real Spanish food.
  cite.credit Photo: Anthony92931
  aside.notes
    ul
      li Turn your back on the room. Walk.
      li The Mexico mix-up pays off here, so don't explain it either.

//- The heel's end: the yes path's lemon, and the address struck through on the click. The room still gets the URL. It just has to read it through a line.
section.lemon-slide.lemon-end(data-background="#e6e924" data-timing="5")
  img(src="svg/lemon.svg" alt="" role="presentation")
  p
    span.fragment.strike
      +link(liveURL)
        | ahoylemon.github.io/color-is-a-lie
  aside.notes
    ul
      li Click: strike the address. They voted.
      li Out by 5:00.
